For+Sophia", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Shadow+Child+Song+For+Sophia", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Shadow+Child+Song+For+Sophia", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Shadow+Child+Song+For+Sophia", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Shadow+Child+Song+For+Sophia&type=all", "search": true}, {"label": "shazam", "url": "https://www.shazam.com/track/883053229", "search": false}], "notes": ["2026 LDN Records"]}, {"t": 6924, "time": "01:55:24", "artist": "Diplo & SIDEPIECE", "title": "On My Mind", "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Diplo+%26+SIDEPIECE+On+My+Mind", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Diplo+%26+SIDEPIECE+On+My+Mind", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Diplo+%26+SIDEPIECE+On+My+Mind", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Diplo+%26+SIDEPIECE+On+My+Mind", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Diplo+%26+SIDEPIECE+On+My+Mind", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Diplo+%26+SIDEPIECE+On+My+Mind", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Diplo+%26+SIDEPIECE+On+My+Mind&type=all", "search": true}, {"label": "shazam", "url": "https://www.shazam.com/track/503827028", "search": false}], "notes": ["2019 FFRR"]}, {"t": 7018, "time": "01:56:58", "artist": "Jack Wickham", "title": "Kotone", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Jack+Wickham+Kotone", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2w4fiEPu5p4", "search": false}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/fuselondon/sets/jack-wickham-kotone-ep-infuse019-vinyl-only", "search": false}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Jack+Wickham+Kotone", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Jack+Wickham+Kotone", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Jack+Wickham+Kotone", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/release/10311375-Jack-Wickham-Kotone-EP", "search": false}], "notes": ["“This is Jack Wickham, a track from, I think it was 2017 maybe, Cotone”", "the audio briefly looked like Tanya Louise - Deep in You (Rob's Vibey Dub), but the presenter said otherwise", "Title track of the 2017 vinyl-only Kotone EP (INFUSE019) on FUSE London's Infuse label, by Leeds producer Jack Wickham."]}], "counts": {"high": 17, "mid": 5, "low": 3}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:06:53", "end": "00:08:31", "text": "Hey, it's Loose Joints on FBi and Tyson Koh here taking over from Mi Hente, my people. Thanks for a great show. Sounding great. A little live set as a treat on your Sunday afternoon. I'm with you until 5pm and we just heard from the Canadian musician Joseph Shabison who was in bands like The War on Drugs and Destroyer, but that was from his album Anne from a few years ago. And right now we're listening to a track called Skyride by Dan Dare. It was released in the late 80s for some kind of library, synthesized library music, keeping things pretty mellow for the start of the show before getting into a bit of a tallow and 80s stuff and picking it up later. I might play something else off Shy One's album that she released this year and also hear from a couple of legendary acts like Cyndi Lauper and The Birds. So don't go anywhere. Hope you're enjoying the day. Sun's come out. it's been a pretty great weekend all things considered we are still in winter but um yeah it's definitely feeling like springs around the corner it's loose joints"}, {"start": "00:26:39", "end": "00:28:46", "text": "Yeah, it's Bach Psychosis, a group that, yeah, post-rock group from London and I was listening to a lot of post-rock in the late 90s, just when I was finishing up high school and this is a band and an album that I think still holds up today. The album Game Over from 1997 and the track Three Girl Rumba and before that we heard from felt um you'd be forgiven for thinking that it was a cocteau tint twins track but um yeah it was produced by robin guthrie and featured the vocals of elizabeth fraser who myself and i know many of you got the privilege to see uh perform with massive attack a couple of weeks ago and so that was their track, Primitive Painters. And in there as well was The Birds for some 60s psych. Out to Dale, the track that I played was Everybody's Been Burnt. And we also heard from Donovan with Clara Clairvoyant. And at the very top, Eddie Suzuki, who was, don't know too much about him um uh japanese hawaiian i believe off an album called high tide from the early 70s and i played beauty near hanalei so yeah i hope you're doing well it's been pretty cruisy thus far i'm going to play some steve hillage in just a tick if you want to text in let me know what you're up to it's 0435 123 945 would love to hear how you're enjoying loose joints today in the car out and about at home but um yeah uh enjoying playing these tunes for you uh it's always a mixed bag so keep it locked fbi"}, {"start": "00:44:56", "end": "00:47:12", "text": "Yeah, an absolute all-time track from The The London Band off the Soul Mining album from 1983. It's called Giant. And it's Tyson Koh here on Loose Joints. And, yeah, just got quite a lot of text in over the last little while, including from Stav and also Peter from Narrenburn, who's having a cruisy day. I mean, that's what Sundays are for. has been doing his tax and also working in the garage on some cars um yeah appreciate your company as well also graham from katoomba who's in bathurst for beetle fest this weekend and can pick up the fbi signal from the top of mount panorama yeah we do have a pretty beefy transmitter i must say definitely the envy of a lot of other community radio stations we go beyond sydney metro by far so glad you're picking us up from there and um yeah also out to the heart mountain crew as well. Thanks for a fabulous weekend. Out to Erin in Victoria. And also in that set played, of course, Cindy Lauper. She's such a special artist for me. Just one of the first musical obsessions as a toddler, for sure. I smashed the She's So Unusual compact disc because my dad was a very early adopter. And, yeah, that track, All Through the Night, a favourite album track of mine. Also, Steve Hillidge with Alone and Bach's Psychosis was at the top. All right, plenty more coming up. Soice Joints."}, {"start": "01:08:46", "end": "01:11:03", "text": "It's Loose Joints, Tyson Koh here and this is Piano Fantasia from 1985, French producer and this track is called Song for Denise and it's the audiophile dance mix. Before that, a singer from Martinique called Jean-Michel Jean-Louis, and yeah, that classic Zouk style, bringing over sounds from the West Indies and the Caribbean, filtered through French diaspora, and yeah, from 1990, that was the track called Jew. and then before that Patrice Russian One of the Greats Without a Doubt and that was the track Don't Blame Me and then also Georgie Red who were a German group and I played the song Help the Man alright so I hope you're enjoying the show I'm always having a good time presenting it for you a couple of texts have come in not signed off so I don't know who's texted but just someone who's loving the left field disco keep it coming and also that they remember hearing Piano Fantasia on a noise in my head mix that Hooney did both legends of the game noise in my head being the person who runs the Efficient Space label A good friend of mine, so always happy to name-check him whenever I get the opportunity on Loose Joints. But yeah, coming up in just a tick. I'll tease it by saying it's an instrumental version of a classic movie song, but also we'll be playing something from Shy One as well and lots more. It's Loose Joints."}, {"start": "01:17:30", "end": "01:19:32", "text": "Oh, those sassy sacks. Yeah, it's obviously the theme to Thunderdome, Mad Max. We Don't Need Another Hero, as done by Terry Britton, who's a British-Australian producer, along with Graeme Lyle, who's one half of Gallagher and Lyle. If you're fans of soft rock like I am, that's quite thrilling. I never knew that he was on the soundtrack. But, yeah, it's a good reminder as well that if you enjoy the music that you hear on FBI, on Loose Joints, on any other show, if you appreciate the fact that FBI even exists, we can only exist with your support. So, please do head to fbi.radio.com to become a supporter of the station. And it's generally about $10 a month, and you can adjust that according to your means. Some people pay more, some people pay a bit less. and it helps us stay on the air. And I know that I have been away for such a long time, but I'm about to go on leave. I haven't taken a holiday yet this year, so I'm going to go travelling for about a month. So I'm going to be, yeah, leaving the show in the capable hands of other FBI presenters. but um yes i will be gone for a few weeks but then back after that in um maybe the last week of september all right i'm gonna play a track by michael peters now he um yeah just made this song as far as i know let me show you how um very special show wasn't ever really properly released but uh yeah it's a good one on loose joints Let's get started."}, {"start": "01:36:40", "end": "01:37:18", "text": "As I said, that was the Erotic Dissidence with Movie Ross and Feel the Beat. Some Belgian new beat from 1988 and oh to be there at the time. Wow. Before that we heard from Shy One off her Mali album released this year. I played Liv Dis Ting, Belt Drives and Michael Peters with Let Me Show You How. Alright, I'm going to keep this vibe going and then maybe speed it up a bit more newer. electronic stuff. But yeah, it's loose joints."}, {"start": "01:58:56", "end": "02:00:01", "text": "Okay. Yeah, that is it for me. This is Jack Wickham, a track from, I think it was 2017 maybe, Cotone. And before that, released this year, Shadow Child with Song for Sophia has a real 808 State vibe to it. and then before that Louis CL with Sick and Trey Risqué featuring Nicky before that with A Night With The Boys and The Trail of Destruction dub and that is it for me as I mentioned earlier I'm going to be taking a few weeks off actually going on Leave Leave which is really exciting and this track is getting me quite g'd up for my time in Berlin which I'm going to be heading to among other places but yeah it should be a lot of fun as usual you can support the station by heading to fbi.radio slash support keeps us on the air including myself and your next host"}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:00:58"}, "track": {"title": "I Thought That I Could Get Away with It", "artists": [{"name": "Joseph Shabason"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:08:46"}, "track": {"title": "Beauty Near Hanalei", "artists": [{"name": "Eddie Suzuki & New Hawaii"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:12:35"}, "track": {"title": "Clara Clairvoyant", "artists": [{"name": "Donovan"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:15:26"}, "track": {"title": "Everybody's Been Burned", "artists": [{"name": "The Byrds"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:18:24"}, "track": {"title": "Primitive Painters", "artists": [{"name": "Felt"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:24:07"}, "track": {"title": "T